        <p>TRM Labs puts Ethereum at about $3.79 billion and Bitcoin at about $1.47 billion, followed by Tron at about $628 million, the XRP Ledger at about $296 million, Solana at about $96 million and other chains at about $77 million (<a href="https://www.trmlabs.com/resources/blog/north-korea-steals-usd-6-36-billion-from-binance-in-the-largest-hack-in-history" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">TRM Labs, 2026</a>). Elliptic independently counts $3.80 billion across 186 tokens on Ethereum alone (<a href="https://www.elliptic.co/insights/binance-largest-hack-in-history/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Elliptic, 2026</a>). These firms sell blockchain investigation products, so Best Answer Hub labels their numbers as vendor estimates rather than audited totals.</p>

        <div class="cav">Check the claim</div>
        <h2 id="biggest">Is the Binance hack the biggest crypto hack ever?</h2>

        <p>Yes, with a qualifier Best Answer Hub thinks you should keep attached: it is the largest crypto theft on record <b>by value at the moment it was taken</b>. Elliptic goes further and calls it "almost certainly the largest single theft of any kind in history". That wider claim is Elliptic's own, and Best Answer Hub has not independently tested it.</p>

